      "receiptId": "yorkshire-curd-tart.html-1",
      "receiptSource": "Original Receipt from Newcastle Evening Chronicle - Wednesday 10 January 1990",
      "receiptText": "\u003Cb\u003EYORKSHIRE CURD TART\u003C/b\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E\n1/2 lb rich shortcrust pastry\u003Cbr\u003E\n1/2 lb curds\u003Cbr\u003E\n4oz caster sugar\u003Cbr\u003E\n2oz currants\u003Cbr\u003E\n2 eggs\u003Cbr\u003E\nJuice and rind of one lemon\u003Cbr\u003E\nGrated nutmeg\u003Cbr\u003E\nRoll out the pastry on a floured board. Line 15-18 patty tins. Mix the curds with the sugar, currants, and beaten egg. Spoon into the patty eases and sprinkle with nutmeg. Bake in a moderate oven for 20-30 minutes until set and golden.\u003Cbr\u003E"
    }
